---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CTASection from '../components/CTASection.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
import { TOPICS } from '../data/taxonomy';

const method = [
  {
    step: 'Question',
    text: 'Start from a specific question about how technology affects people, not from a tool or a technique.',
  },
  {
    step: 'Evidence',
    text: 'Gather what can be documented: public sources, research, and data from controlled environments.',
  },
  {
    step: 'Analysis',
    text: 'Work out what the evidence supports, and say clearly what remains uncertain.',
  },
  {
    step: 'Experiment',
    text: 'Where it helps, build or test something to see how the problem behaves in practice.',
  },
  {
    step: 'Insight',
    text: 'Explain what I learned and why it matters to the people affected.',
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="Why FalconProSec exists: a software engineer investigating how technology and AI affect human trust, safety, identity and opportunity."
>
  <PageHeader
    kicker="About"
    title="Technology is a tool. Human impact is the reason."
    description={`${SITE.name} is my research and experimentation space for the problems emerging where software, AI, cybersecurity and human behavior meet.`}
  />

  <div class="container-site mt-16 space-y-20">
    <section class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.6fr]" aria-labelledby="who">
      <h2 id="who" class="text-2xl font-semibold sm:text-3xl">
        Where I'm coming from
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
        <p>
          I'm Sandra. My background is in computer science and software
          engineering, so I understand technology from the side of the people
          who build it: the decisions, the trade-offs, and the shortcuts that
          seem harmless at the time.
        </p>
        <p>
          Over time I became more interested in the other side: what happens
          when that technology reaches real people. That is why I'm expanding
          into cybersecurity, AI, investigation and security research. I'm not
          trying to collect specialties. I'm following a problem, and these are
          the tools it needs.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.6fr]" aria-labelledby="why">
      <h2 id="why" class="text-2xl font-semibold sm:text-3xl">
        Why human impact
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
        <p>
          Most software is built to solve a customer's problem. I want to solve
          human problems: the ones that show up when a scam sounds exactly like
          a family member, when an automated system makes a decision nobody can
          explain, or when a hospital or school loses access to its own
          systems.
        </p>
        <p>
          As AI gets more capable, it can generate convincing voices, faces,
          messages and evidence, which makes human trust both harder to protect
          and more worth protecting. The same technology could also make
          education, accessibility and protection available to far more
          people. I want to understand both sides, ideally before the problems
          become impossible to ignore.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="areas">
      <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.6fr]">
        <h2 id="areas" class="text-2xl font-semibold sm:text-3xl">
          What I investigate
        </h2>
        <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
          My work is organized around problems, not job titles. These six areas
          are not career tracks. They're questions I keep returning to, and
          some of them don't fit neatly into any existing role.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ul class="mt-8 grid gap-px overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-line bg-line sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
        {
          TOPICS.map((t) => (
            <li class="bg-ink p-6">
              <a href={`/topics/${t.slug}`} class="font-heading font-semibold text-white hover:text-primary-text">
                {t.label}
              </a>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">{t.description}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="method">
      <p class="kicker !text-primary-text">The approach</p>
      <h2 id="method" class="mt-3 text-2xl font-semibold sm:text-3xl">
        How I investigate
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-muted">
        These are not answers I already have. They're questions I'm willing to
        investigate, in the open.
      </p>
      <ol class="mt-8 grid gap-px overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-line bg-line sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-5">
        {
          method.map((m, i) => (
            <li class="bg-ink p-6">
              <span class="font-mono text-sm text-primary-text">
                {String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}
              </span>
              <p class="mt-3 font-heading font-semibold text-white">{m.step}</p>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">{m.text}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.6fr]" aria-labelledby="what-it-is">
      <h2 id="what-it-is" class="text-2xl font-semibold sm:text-3xl">
        What this is, and isn't
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
        <p>
          {SITE.name} is a personal, independent space. It is not a security
          company and does not offer professional services. I'm not claiming
          to be an expert in AI security, cybersecurity or psychology. I'm
          building the technical and investigative ability to work on these
          problems, and showing that work as I go.
        </p>
        <p>
          Expect questions, experiments, sources you can check yourself, and an
          honest account of what I learned, including when the answer is
          "it's complicated".
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.6fr]" aria-labelledby="corrections">
      <h2 id="corrections" class="text-2xl font-semibold sm:text-3xl">
        Corrections
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
        <p>
          Mistakes happen. When I find an error in an investigation or article,
          I correct it on the page and note it in a visible “Corrections &
          updates” section with the date, rather than changing it silently.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you notice something wrong or have more context,
          <a href="/contact?reason=correction" class="link">please get in touch</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <CTASection
      title="Start with a question"
      description="Read what I'm investigating, or suggest a question about technology and people that deserves a closer look."
      primary={{ href: '/investigations', label: 'Explore Investigations' }}
      secondary={{ href: '/contact?reason=investigation', label: 'Suggest a question' }}
    />
  </div>
</Layout>
